feat(graph-vcs): verify M6 TerminusStore against a live server + shared parity contract

The TerminusDB backend shipped in the session-manager commit had never run
against a real server. Booting terminusdb/terminusdb-server:v12.0.7 surfaced
three bugs, fixed here:

- TerminusStore::new auto-provisions its organization (POST
  /api/organization) before database/schema — a fresh server only has the
  admin org, so every open previously failed.
- Document writes switch from POST overwrite=true (which *appends* field
  values, corrupting single-valued fields like branch heads into sets) to
  PUT create=true (true replace/upsert).
- Chart image corrected: terminusdb/terminusdb does not exist on Docker
  Hub; pinned terminusdb/terminusdb-server:v12.0.7.

Parity tests: the ten store-level scenarios move into graph_vcs::contract
(feature contract, mirroring the session-manager conformance suite) and run
identically against MinigrafStore (always) and TerminusStore via
tests/terminus_contract.rs — env-gated on TERMINUSDB_TEST_URL, or
TERMINUSDB_BOOT_CONTAINER=docker|podman to boot the pinned image and run
the whole contract plus a reopen-persistence check; auto-skip otherwise, so
cargo test -p graph-vcs --all-features stays green with no container
runtime. Verified green against podman-booted TerminusDB.

Docs: M6 marked done in docs/session-manager-plan.md with the verification
findings; AGENTS.md crate map updated.
